    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d487">

                <pb facs="0863" n="849" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg849"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.CC/9–2844</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Halifax</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 598</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-28">September 28,
                        1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honour to inform you, with
                    reference to my note number 473 of August 1st., under instructions from His
                    Majesty’s Principal Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs, that Sir Alexander
                    Cadogan, G.C.M.G., K.C.B., Permanent Under Secretary of State for Foreign
                    Affairs, is expected to leave Washington shortly for the United Kingdom,
                    accompanied by Sir William Malkin, G.C.M.G., C.B., K.G., Mr. Peter Loxley,
                    Colonel Capel Dunn, Mr. A. H. Poynton, and Mr. Paul Falla.</p>
                <p>After their departure the Delegation to continue talks with the United States and
                    Chinese Delegations<anchor n="57" xml:id="d487-f1"/> will consist of the
                    following, with myself in charge:<anchor n="58" xml:id="d487-f2"/>
                    <list>
                        <item>Admiral Sir Percy Noble,<anchor n="59" xml:id="d487-f3"/>
                        </item>
                        <item>Lieutenant General G. N. Macready,</item>
                        <item>Air Marshal Sir William Welch,<anchor n="60" xml:id="d487-f4"/>
                        </item>
                        <item>Sir George Sansom<anchor n="61" xml:id="d487-f5"/>
                        </item>
                        <item>Mr. Gladwyn Jebb</item>
                        <item>Professor C. K. Webster</item>
                        <item>Mr. Paul Gore-Booth</item>
                        <item>Mr. A. It. K. Mackenzie (Press Officer)</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d487-f1" n="57" xml:id="d487-f1-content">
                <p>For lists of American and Chinese representatives during the
                    Anglo-American-Chinese phase of discussions, see announcement to the press by
                    the Acting Secretary of State on August 1, and letter of August 21 from the
                    Chinese Ambassador, <ref target="#pg698">pp. 698</ref> and <ref target="#pg712"
                        >712</ref>, respectively.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d487-f2" n="58" xml:id="d487-f2-content">
                <p>The British Ambassador informed the Secretary of State on September 28 and 30 of
                    the two following additions to the list of United Kingdom Delegation: Maj. Gen.
                    Grove-White and Berkeley Gage, a member of the British Foreign Office.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d487-f3" n="59" xml:id="d487-f3-content">
                <p>He was succeeded shortly by Commodore A. W. Clarke.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d487-f4" n="60" xml:id="d487-f4-content">
                <p>He was succeeded shortly by Air Vice-Marshal H. P. Willock.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d487-f5" n="61" xml:id="d487-f5-content">
                <p>Minister, Adviser on Far Eastern Affairs, British Embassy in the United
                    States.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
